  "readings": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "XC04111",
    "sub_id": "GM674",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpc_seq": 1,
    "tpc_book": "<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:500px\">\n\t<caption>教科書 (書名、作者、書局/代理商、說明)</caption>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>書名</th>\n\t\t\t<th>作者</th>\n\t\t\t<th>書局/代理商</th>\n\t\t\t<th>說明</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>莫札特：費加洛的婚姻</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>吳祖強 主編</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>世界文物出版社</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>《費加洛的婚姻》是根據法國劇作家博馬舍的同名話劇改編，屬博馬舍所作「費加洛三部曲」的第二部。這部歌頌下等人物聰明機智，譏諷封建制度的話劇引起了軒然大波，而遭皇帝禁演。經過某些刪減又改成歌劇後，才得以上演。《費加洛的婚姻》可說是世界歌劇史上最優秀的腳本之一。</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>Mozart: Le nozze di Figaro</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>達蓬特（L. da Ponte） 劇本</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Mercury Publishing House</td>\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n",
    "tpc_book_en": "<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th><strong>book title</strong></th>\n\t\t\t<th>author</th>\n\t\t\t<th>bookstore / distributor</th>\n\t\t\t<th>description</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart: <em>The Marriage of Figaro</em></td>\n\t\t\t<td>Edited by Wu Zuqiang</td>\n\t\t\t<td>World Cultural Relics Publishing House</td>\n\t\t\t<td><em>The Marriage of Figaro</em> is based on the play of the same name by the French playwright Pierre Beaumarchais and is the second part of Beaumarchais&rsquo;s &ldquo;Figaro Trilogy.&rdquo;<br />\n\t\t\tThe play, which praises the intelligence and wit of lower-class characters while satirizing the feudal system, caused a great controversy and was banned by the emperor. Only after certain cuts and adaptations into an opera was it finally allowed to be performed.<br />\n\t\t\t<em>The Marriage of Figaro</em> is considered one of the finest librettos in the history of world opera.</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>Mozart: Le nozze di Figaro</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Lorenzo Da Ponte &mdash; libretto</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Mercury Publishing House</td>\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n"
  },
